{"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"major":0,"patch":0},"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"tokens":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"minimumSpanningArborescence"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"kind":"genericParameter","text":"W"},{"kind":"text","text":">("},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"weight"},{"kind":"text","text":": ("},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Self"},{"kind":"text","text":"."},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols08DirectedA0P5EdgesQa","text":"Edges","identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/DirectedGraph\/Edges-swift.associatedtype"},{"kind":"text","text":"."},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:Sl5IndexQa","text":"Index"},{"kind":"text","text":") -> "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"W"},{"kind":"text","text":") -> "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:13SpanningTrees9BranchingV","text":"Branching","identifier":"doc:\/\/SpanningTrees\/documentation\/SpanningTrees\/Branching"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Self"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"W"},{"kind":"text","text":">? "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"where"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"W"},{"kind":"text","text":" : "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:s18AdditiveArithmeticP","text":"AdditiveArithmetic"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"W"},{"kind":"text","text":" : "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:SL","text":"Comparable"}],"platforms":["Linux"],"languages":["swift"]}]},{"content":[{"anchor":"return-value","text":"Return Value","type":"heading","level":2},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The arborescence’s edges, in position order, and their total weight. Its root is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the one vertex no edge enters."}],"type":"paragraph"}],"kind":"content"},{"content":[{"type":"heading","anchor":"discussion","text":"Discussion","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The search runs once, from an added root joined to every vertex by an edge that costs more"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"than any set of real edges, so the answer uses exactly one of them when a spanning"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"arborescence exists. Self-loops are never weighed; every other edge is weighed once."}]},{"type":"aside","style":"note","name":"Complexity","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"O(m log m + n log n)."}]}]},{"type":"aside","style":"note","name":"Precondition","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Every weight is finite; the differences between weights do not overflow;"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"for a weight type that is not "},{"code":"SignedNumeric","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", the sum of all the weights fits."}]}]}],"kind":"content"}],"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/spanningtrees\/graphprotocols\/directedgraph\/minimumspanningarborescence(weight:)"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/SpanningTrees\/documentation\/SpanningTrees\/GraphProtocols\/DirectedGraph\/minimumSpanningArborescence(weight:)","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"sections":[],"metadata":{"externalID":"s:14GraphProtocols08DirectedA0P13SpanningTreesE07minimumD12Arborescence6weightAD9BranchingVyxqd__GSgqd__5Edges_5IndexQZXE_ts18AdditiveArithmeticRd__SLRd__lF","roleHeading":"Instance Method","symbolKind":"method","title":"minimumSpanningArborescence(weight:)","modules":[{"name":"SpanningTrees","relatedModules":["GraphProtocols"]}],"extendedModule":"GraphProtocols","remoteSource":{"fileName":"Edmonds.swift","url":"https:\/\/github.com\/Tyler-Keith-Thompson\/Grafluent\/blob\/main\/Sources\/SpanningTrees\/Edmonds.swift#L89"},"role":"symbol","fr